      "id": "qjnucok",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Meaning of Heat"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Heat is a form of energy that flows from a body at a higher temperature to a body at a lower temperature.",
        "Temperature is the measure of the degree of hotness or coldness of an object.",
        "Conduction is the primary mode of heat transfer in solids where energy passes without actual movement of particles.",
        "Convection occurs in liquids and gases through the actual physical movement of molecules.",
        "Radiation is heat transfer via electromagnetic waves that requires no material medium.",
        "Thermal expansion causes solids, liquids, and gases to expand upon heating."
      ],
      "id": "4uc1gt8"
    },
